From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 22:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] VideoRenderers: draw subtitles at a chosen brightness

Subtitles come out as bright as whoever made them chose, and on HDR output
that can be far brighter than the picture around them: the English SDH
track of one UHD disc authors its text at PQ 154, about 253 nits, where the
interface's own white sits near 200.

Add Player > Subtitles > Brightness: the most light a subtitle may have, in
nits, 10 to 400 in steps of 10, or "As authored". Default 100. It is a
ceiling: a subtitle authored brighter is dimmed to it, one authored dimmer
keeps its light, and the brightness is measured on the colours the subtitle
actually draws with.

- An image subtitle authored in HDR, drawn as PQ, is measured on the palette
  entries its bitmap uses - a PGS palette lives for a whole epoch and keeps
  what earlier subtitles drew with; one UHD disc carries a full-PQ, 10000-nit
  entry beside its 244-nit text. Objects shown together share one measure,
  so a caption and a dimmer line beside it keep their contrast. The palette
  is scaled in linear light through the PQ curve and rounded down, so nothing
  comes out above the value asked for.
- Every other subtitle is sRGB by the time it is drawn: text through libass,
  SDR image subtitles, an HDR one converted for SDR output. Its white is the
  interface's while the HDR composite converts the interface, 203 nits on
  other HDR output and 120 on SDR; its brightest colour is measured against
  that and scaled in linear light through the sRGB curve. It cannot be drawn
  brighter than that white. Text is scaled while libass's output is turned
  into a texture and put back afterwards, so libass's own change detection
  still sees the frame it made.

Alpha is left alone throughout, so edges and transparency do not change.
Blu-ray menus are marked as such and keep their light, as do Kodi's own
overlays such as the player debug information. DVD disc subpictures take
another path and are not covered.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
---
